window.GAMEDAY_FINDINGS = [{"title":"A node rejecting the network's chain raised no alert","text":"Invalidating the tip on testnet4 moved the node onto a competing fork without a sound. A node that rejects the chain its peers build on keeps headers equal to blocks, because bitcoind drops headers that build on an invalid block, so BitcoindBlocksBehindHeaders could never fire. Only the 95-minute no-new-blocks warning would have, as a ticket. In the drill the node fell 7 blocks behind.","fix":"the exporter now reports the highest invalid chain tip, and the new critical alert BitcoindRejectedChainAhead paged 10m 44s after the fault."},{"title":"A busy bitcoind stopped electrs","text":"When bitcoind's RPC work queue filled up, it answered 503 'Work queue depth exceeded', and electrs exited: 'server failed: request failed HTTP/1.1 503 Service Unavailable'. electrs waits and retries when bitcoind is unreachable or still starting, but any other HTTP status is a plain error, which ends its main loop. A traffic spike on bitcoind becomes an indexer outage.","label":"Patch","fix":"electrs treats a 503 like a dropped connection and retries (a small change with a unit test against a fake bitcoind), ready to send upstream to Blockstream/electrs."},{"title":"A fast OOM loop was invisible to the memory and restart alerts","text":"Under a 300 MiB limit electrs was killed 31 times in 8 minutes, each time within seconds of starting and before Prometheus could scrape it. ElectrsMemoryHigh and ElectrsRestartLoop never had a sample. Only ElectrsDown paged, after 5m 52s, without saying why.","fix":"BitcoinNodeOOMKilled opens a ticket from the kernel's OOM counter, or from a container's OOMKilled exit on Kubernetes, so the cause arrives with the page."},{"title":"One missing exporter paged twice","text":"With the bitcoind scrape job gone, the job-has-no-target check and the half-a-pair-missing check both fired with different labels, so Alertmanager sent two pages for one fault.","fix":"the job-level check now fires only when the other job has no targets either. A rerun paged once; the replay shows the original run with both pages."},{"title":"A removed scrape job pages after 10 minutes, not 5","text":"After the config reload Prometheus 3.15.1 kept serving the job's last sample for 5 minutes, so the alert's 5-minute wait only started after that.","label":"Documented","fix":"in the bitcoind-down runbook: after a config change, expect the page late and check the change first."}];
